  </diagram>
  <diagram id="m2-crc-notes" name="M2 - Relationship Rationale">
    <mxGraphModel grid="0" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1123" pageHeight="794" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="r-title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=26;" value="&lt;b&gt;SideQuest&lt;/b&gt; | M2 relationship rationale" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1047" x="38" y="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r-intro" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=15;" value="A, B and C refer to the M2 CRC page. This is the agreed P4-style conceptual model updated for current code." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="37" width="1047" x="38" y="83" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;shape=rectangle;fillColor=#FBF5EE;strokeColor=#8B4B10;strokeWidth=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="479" width="335" x="38" y="133" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="head0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=16;fontColor=#8B4B10;" value="A / EventCatalog groups Events" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="311" x="50" y="145" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-left0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8B4B10;" value="EventCatalog" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="105" x="50" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-right0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8B4B10;" value="Event" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="118" x="243" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-edge0" edge="1" parent="1" source="sample-left0" style="html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=.5;entryX=0;entryY=.5;startArrow=diamondThin;startFill=0;startSize=15;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#8B4B10;" target="sample-right0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="body0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Meaning.&lt;/b&gt; The EventCatalog is a shared public collection. It exposes create(draft), listUpcoming() and getById(id). The underlying EventTable adapter stores public Events; a Node API shields database keys from browsers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why a hollow diamond?&lt;/b&gt; Posted Events have independent persistence in the shared SQL table. Discarding an adapter or clearing a screen must never delete them. The original professor-approved P4 ownership notation is retained.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Card implementation.&lt;/b&gt; The TypeScript catalog is an interface plus Model functions, not an instantiable UML class. This diagram expresses CRC responsibilities." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="375" width="311" x="50" y="210" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;shape=rectangle;fillColor=#EFF7F3;strokeColor=#116B59;strokeWidth=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="479" width="335" x="394" y="133" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="head1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=16;fontColor=#116B59;" value="B / Schedule uses EventCatalog" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="311" x="406" y="145" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-left1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#116B59;" value="Schedule" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="105" x="406" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-right1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#116B59;" value="EventCatalog" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="118" x="599" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-edge1" edge="1" parent="1" source="sample-left1" style="html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=.5;entryX=0;entryY=.5;dashed=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=open;endFill=0;endSize=10;strokeColor=#116B59;" target="sample-right1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="body1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Meaning.&lt;/b&gt; Personal plans are device-local Event ID strings. The sharedSchedule Controller asks EventCatalog.getById(id) to resolve those IDs, including events older than the upcoming browse list.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why the dashed dependency?&lt;/b&gt; Schedule behavior needs catalog lookup, but the catalog does not own plans and the schedule does not own Event records. In code the Controller mediates the call.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure behavior.&lt;/b&gt; Failed or timed-out lookups preserve saved IDs; successful null results identify missing Events." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="375" width="311" x="406" y="225" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;shape=rectangle;fillColor=#EFF7F3;strokeColor=#116B59;strokeWidth=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="479" width="335" x="750" y="133" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="head2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=16;fontColor=#116B59;" value="C / Schedule references Events" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="311" x="762" y="145" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-left2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#116B59;" value="Schedule" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="105" x="762" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-right2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#116B59;" value="Event" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25" width="118" x="955" y="184" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sample-edge2" edge="1" parent="1" source="sample-left2" style="html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=.5;entryX=0;entryY=.5;startArrow=diamondThin;startFill=0;startSize=15;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#116B59;" target="sample-right2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="body2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Meaning.&lt;/b&gt; One browser maintains zero or more distinct planned Event IDs under sidequest.planned-event-ids.v1, provisionally capped at 100.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why a hollow diamond?&lt;/b&gt; Removing a plan never deletes the public Event. Many devices may independently plan the same Event. The local list records references rather than copies of public records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Time rules.&lt;/b&gt; The Model sorts resolved Events chronologically and warns about overlaps; adjoining events are allowed. The dependency is logical, not an SQL foreign key." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="375" width="311" x="762" y="225" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="shared-explanation" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=13;fillColor=#EDF3FA;strokeColor=#254F88;spacing=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;READING THE M2 DIAGRAM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Three conceptual CRC roles match the accepted P4: Event, EventCatalog and Schedule. Browser Views and coordinating Controllers are implementation layers, not new domain classes. Public events use one SQL table; the personal schedule is a separate browser JSON list. Free-time search is transient. The ER diagram documents the two storage boundaries explicitly." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="1047" x="38" y="619" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Georgia;fontSize=14;fontColor=#202E40;spacing=0;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Evidence:&lt;/b&gt; app/src/model/eventCatalog.ts, schedule.ts, events.ts; controller/sharedSchedule.ts; SQL migration; original P4 design." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="22" width="1047" x="38" y="760" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
